{"event":"findings_submitted","payload":{"findings":[{"category":"concurrency","claim":"Dead-letter requeue is not atomic with its state check and can fail or produce an inconsistent result when purge runs concurrently.","evidence":"Lines 68-74 perform an unlocked read/check; lines 76-83 issue independent writes; lines 84-85 assume the row still exists. storage.purge_terminal deletes DONE/DEAD rows without coordinating with this sequence (storage.py:240-245).","file":"src/taskq/deadletter.py","id":"TQ-001","line_end":86,"line_start":66,"root_cause":"The method reads the task, checks DEAD, then performs reset_attempts and mark_state as separate autocommit statements without a write transaction or conditional UPDATE. purge_terminal can delete the row between these operations; the subsequent get returns None and triggers an AssertionError. Concurrent administrative operations therefore turn a valid requeue request into a server error.","severity":"medium","suggested_verification":"Run requeue and purge concurrently against the same DEAD task, or inject a delete between the initial get and reset_attempts; observe the assertion/500 response."}]},"schema_version":"0.2.0","seq":38,"ts":"2026-08-29T15:50:09.355+00:00"}
